@startuml
title querychat: Filter Flow (update_dashboard)

actor User
participant "Shiny UI\n(Browser)" as UI
participant "Shiny Server\n(Python)" as Server
participant "querychat" as QC
participant "DuckDB" as DB
participant "LLM API" as LLM

== App startup ==
Server -> QC : QueryChat(df, "titanic", ...)
QC -> DB : CREATE TABLE titanic\n(data loaded into DuckDB)
QC --> Server : qc_vals\n(.df()  .sql  .title())

== User: "Show only survivors" ==
User -> UI : types message in chat sidebar
UI -> Server : on_user_submit()
Server -> QC : stream_response_async()

QC -> LLM : system_prompt + chat_history\n+ "Show only survivors"

note right of LLM
  System prompt includes:
  • table schema
  • data_description
  • extra_instructions
  • 3 tool definitions

  NO data rows
end note

LLM --> QC : **tool_call:**\nquerychat_update_dashboard(\n  query = "SELECT * FROM titanic\n           WHERE survived = 1",\n  title = "Survivors only"\n)

QC -> DB : validate + execute SQL
DB --> QC : ✅ valid

QC --> LLM : "Dashboard updated.\nUse query tool to review\nresults, if needed."

note over QC #FFEEEE
  LLM gets ONLY this string.
  No rows, no counts, no stats.
end note

== Shiny reactive chain ==
QC -> Server : state.sql set\n→ qc_vals.sql invalidated
Server -> DB : qc_vals.df() re-runs SQL
DB --> Server : filtered DataFrame
Server --> UI : re-render table + title

LLM --> QC : text reply (if any)
QC --> Server : stream chunks
Server --> UI : append to chat sidebar

UI --> User : updated table\n+ "Survivors only" title

@enduml
